            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-42583",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "netty: io.netty/netty-codec-compression: io.netty/netty-codec: Netty: Denial of Service via excessive memory allocation in LZ4FrameDecoder"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Netty is an asynchronous, event-driven network application framework. Prior to 4.2.13.Final and 4.1.133.Final, Lz4FrameDecoder allocates a ByteBuf of size decompressedLength (up to 32 MB per block) before LZ4 runs. A peer only needs a 21-byte header plus compressedLength payload bytes - 22 bytes if compressedLength == 1 - to force that allocation. This vulnerability is fixed in 4.2.13.Final and 4.1.133.Final."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42583",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-42583\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: io.netty:netty-codec\nFixed Version: 4.1.133.Final\nLink: [CVE-2026-42583](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42583)\nNetty is an asynchronous, event-driven network application framework. Prior to 4.2.13.Final and 4.1.133.Final, Lz4FrameDecoder allocates a ByteBuf of size decompressedLength (up to 32 MB per block) before LZ4 runs. A peer only needs a 21-byte header plus compressedLength payload bytes - 22 bytes if compressedLength == 1 - to force that allocation. This vulnerability is fixed in 4.2.13.Final and 4.1.133.Final.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-42583**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|io.netty:netty-codec|4.1.133.Final|[CVE-2026-42583](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42583)|\n\nNetty is an asynchronous, event-driven network application framework. Prior to 4.2.13.Final and 4.1.133.Final, Lz4FrameDecoder allocates a ByteBuf of size decompressedLength (up to 32 MB per block) before LZ4 runs. A peer only needs a 21-byte header plus compressedLength payload bytes - 22 bytes if compressedLength == 1 - to force that allocation. This vulnerability is fixed in 4.2.13.Final and 4.1.133.Final."
              },
              "properties": {
