              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "netty-codec-redis: Netty: Command injection via CRLF characters in Redis codec encoder"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Netty is an asynchronous, event-driven network application framework. Prior to 4.2.13.Final and 4.1.133.Final, the Netty Redis codec encoder (RedisEncoder) writes user-controlled string content directly to the network output buffer without validating or sanitizing CRLF (\\r\\n) characters. Since the Redis Serialization Protocol (RESP) uses CRLF as the command/response delimiter, an attacker who can control the content of a Redis message can inject arbitrary Redis commands or forge fake responses. This vulnerability is fixed in 4.2.13.Final and 4.1.133.Final."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42586",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-42586\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: io.netty:netty-codec-redis\nFixed Version: 4.2.13.Final, 4.1.133.Final\nLink: [CVE-2026-42586](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42586)\nNetty is an asynchronous, event-driven network application framework. Prior to 4.2.13.Final and 4.1.133.Final, the Netty Redis codec encoder (RedisEncoder) writes user-controlled string content directly to the network output buffer without validating or sanitizing CRLF (\\r\\n) characters. Since the Redis Serialization Protocol (RESP) uses CRLF as the command/response delimiter, an attacker who can control the content of a Redis message can inject arbitrary Redis commands or forge fake responses. This vulnerability is fixed in 4.2.13.Final and 4.1.133.Final.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-42586**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|io.netty:netty-codec-redis|4.2.13.Final, 4.1.133.Final|[CVE-2026-42586](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42586)|\n\nNetty is an asynchronous, event-driven network application framework. Prior to 4.2.13.Final and 4.1.133.Final, the Netty Redis codec encoder (RedisEncoder) writes user-controlled string content directly to the network output buffer without validating or sanitizing CRLF (\\r\\n) characters. Since the Redis Serialization Protocol (RESP) uses CRLF as the command/response delimiter, an attacker who can control the content of a Redis message can inject arbitrary Redis commands or forge fake responses. This vulnerability is fixed in 4.2.13.Final and 4.1.133.Final."
              },
